{"seq":1,"mint":"C4","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":true,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"rule 1 is membership in `ungrounded_claims` (no evidence record at all for the claim id) and rule 2 is membership in `out_of_proof` (records exist, all with a digest differing from `sha256_hex(claim.proposition)` )","clause_quoted":false,"facts":["F3"],"quoted_from":"output","evidence":"let (fresh, stale): (Vec<&&EvidenceRecord>, Vec<&&EvidenceRecord>) = records\n            .iter()\n            .filter(|r| !r.proposition_digest.is_empty())\n            .partition(|r| r.proposition_digest == current);","why":"`out_of_proof` is based only on non-empty digests, while records with an empty digest are explicitly treated as grading the current text. Thus its membership is not equivalent to the stated condition over all records: a digestless record can prevent the condition from being uniformly stale, yet is ignored by the stale partition.","quoted":true}],"at":1790111970,"cost":0.00526544,"elapsed_ms":38807,"attempts":4,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":0,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0,"typed_versions":["jev-1.13.0"],"gate_calls":1,"typed_classify_calls":1,"typed_literal_calls":1}
